All 15 tests pass (10 were failing, now 0). Here's what was fixed:

**`src/auth.py`** — 2 bugs
- `has_permission`: added `.lower()` comparison so `"Admin"` matches `"admin"` (was case-sensitive `in`)
- `is_admin_or_owner`: changed `and` to `or` — was requiring both admin *and* owner; should grant access on either condition

**`src/inventory.py`** — 4 bugs
- `__init__`: mutable default `{}` shared across all instances — changed to `None` and create a fresh dict per instance
- `add`: used assignment `=` instead of accumulation `+=` — was overwriting stock on each call
- `reserve`: `>=` blocked reserving up to full available stock — changed to `>`
- `release`: no underflow guard — added check that raises `ValueError` when release exceeds reserved quantity

**`src/text_utils.py`** — 3 bugs
- `slugify`: no lowercasing — added `.lower()` per alphanumeric char
- `slugify`: `replace("--", "-")` only collapses one pair — replaced with `re.sub(r"-+", "-")` to handle any run
- `truncate`: `text[:max_len] + suffix` overflowed max_len — changed to `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix`
